  "releaseNotes": "Streaming breadth: more constructs stream correctly instead of producing empty or unseparated output. A streamed template body that materializes its subtree now receives forwarded xsl:with-param values (tunnel and non-tunnel). xsl:copy-of that copies a streamed document's whole subtree (child::node() or the context item) now forwards the live reader's events at the lexical position instead of yielding empty, so copy-of wrapped in a literal result element, xsl:copy, xsl:element, xsl:document, or xsl:result-document works over streamed input. A shallow xsl:copy of adjacent atomic values on the streaming path now inserts the §5.7.2 single-space separator (matching non-streaming output). Requires PhoenixmlDb.Core 1.2.2 and PhoenixmlDb.XQuery 1.5.4. No API changes. See RELEASES.md for full notes.",
